    "title": "Jack Cress leaves legacy of service and leadership - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By LISA ALMARAZ lalmaraz@sixriversmedia.com ,\n21 hours ago Jack Cress of Mountain View Service Station & Garage and Founding member of TTTA. — Jack Cress (Jack Edwin Cress), 70 of Mountain City and owner of Mountain View Service Station and Garage at 214 W. Main St. age 70 passed away suddenly on Sunday Sept. 20 2026 at 11:45 a.m. due to a cardiac event and subsequent vehicle crash on U.S. 421. He was a leader in the towing operator industry and helped form the TTTA and served them for 22 years. Read full article",
